@page "{id:guid}"
@using MerkaiTrial.Domain.Entities
@model MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages.Leads.ConvertToDealModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Convert to deal";
    var stages = Model.Stages.OrderBy(s => s.SortOrder).ToList();
}
@* =====================================================================
   Leads/ConvertToDeal.cshtml   (031 — rebuild)
   Location: MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web/Pages/Leads/ConvertToDeal.cshtml

   COMPLETE FILE — replaces the existing one.

   WHAT WAS WRONG

   1. ★ THE PIPELINE STAGES WERE HARDCODED, with invented probabilities:

          <option value="Discovery">🔍 Discovery (20% probability)</option>
          <option value="Qualification" selected>✅ Qualification (50% probability)</option>
          <option value="Proposal">📄 Proposal (40% probability)</option>
          <option value="Negotiation">🤝 Negotiation (60% probability)</option>

      Rounds 019 and 020 made stages tenant-configurable — renamed,
      reordered, added, retired. This page ignored all of it. A workspace
      whose stages are Enquiry / Site Visit / Quote / Won was offered four
      stages that do not exist in its pipeline, and the conversion was
      refused by the server.

      Note the probabilities too: Proposal at 40% sat BELOW Qualification
      at 50%, so the numbers were not just unconfigurable, they were wrong.
      They are the tenant's own figures now.

   2. ★ @@GetCurrencySymbol(Model.TenantCurrencySymbol) — the local
      @@functions helper took an ISO CODE ("INR") and was being handed the
      SYMBOL ("₹"). Nothing matched, so it fell through to
      `_ => currencyCode ?? "$"` and returned its own input. It worked by
      accident and would have printed "$" for any tenant whose symbol
      lookup failed. The @@functions block is gone; the page model resolves
      the symbol for the LEAD's currency, which is what the deal is raised
      in.

   3. The form posted Input.Currency as a hidden field and the server
      trusted it. Currency decides what the customer is billed, so it is
      resolved server-side now — see change 4 in ConvertToDeal.cshtml.cs.

   4. "What Happens Next" claimed the lead's status would change to
      "Converted" — our key, not the tenant's word for it.
   ===================================================================== *@

<style>
    .lc { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .lc-back { font-size: .82rem; color: #64748b; text-decoration: none; }
    .lc-back:hover { color: #334155; }
    .lc-title { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin: .35rem 0 0; line-height: 1.2; }
    .lc-sub { font-size: .84rem; color: #64748b; margin: .2rem 0 1rem; }

    .lc-card { border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .lc-card > h2 { font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #64748b;
                    font-weight: 650; margin: 0; padding: .7rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f3f5;
                    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
    .lc-card .bd { padding: 1rem; }

    .lc-lead { border-left: 5px solid #198754; }
    .lc-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: .3rem .9rem; font-size: .86rem; }
    .lc-facts dt { color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 500; }
    .lc-facts dd { margin: 0; color: #0f172a; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

    .lc-money { position: relative; }
    .lc-money .sym { position: absolute; left: 11px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%);
                     font-weight: 650; color: #64748b; pointer-events: none; }
    .lc-money input { padding-left: 34px; }

    /* Stage picker: real radios styled as chips — focusable, announced, and
       working with no script. */
    .lc-stages { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; }
    .lc-stage input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
    .lc-stage span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem; cursor: pointer;
                     padding: .45rem .8rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 2px solid #e9ecef;
                     background: #f8fafc; font-size: .86rem; font-weight: 600; color: #334155; }
    .lc-stage span:hover { border-color: #cbd5e1; }
    .lc-stage input:checked + span { border-color: #4f46e5; background: #fff;
                                     box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(79,70,229,.18); }
    .lc-stage input:focus-visible + span { outline: 2px solid #4f46e5; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .lc-stage .pct { font-weight: 500; color: #94a3b8; font-size: .78rem; }

    .lc-next { font-size: .86rem; }
    .lc-next li { margin-bottom: .35rem; }

    .lc-bar { display: flex; gap: .5rem; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap;
              border-top: 1px solid #e9ecef; padding-top: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }

    @@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
        .lc-title { font-size: 1.25rem; }
        .lc-bar { justify-content: stretch; }
        .lc-bar > * { flex: 1 1 100%; }
        .lc-bar .btn { width: 100%; }
    }
</style>

<div class="lc">

    <a href="/Leads/Detail/@Model.LeadId" class="lc-back">
        <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i>Back to @Model.LeadName
    </a>
    <h1 class="lc-title">Convert to a deal</h1>
    <p class="lc-sub">
        This creates a deal in your pipeline and closes the lead out.
    </p>

    @* TempData alerts are rendered once, globally, by _Layout.cshtml. This
       block is only for ModelState errors, which TempData does not carry. *@
    @if (!ViewData.ModelState.IsValid && ViewData.ModelState[string.Empty]?.Errors.Count > 0)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-warning d-flex gap-2" role="alert">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill mt-1"></i>
            <div>
                @foreach (var err in ViewData.ModelState[string.Empty]!.Errors)
                {
                    <div>@err.ErrorMessage</div>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    <form method="post" asp-route-id="@Model.LeadId">
        <div class="row g-3">

            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <div class="lc-card lc-lead">
                    <h2><i class="bi bi-person-check"></i>The lead</h2>
                    <div class="bd">
                        <dl class="lc-facts mb-0">
                            <dt>Name</dt>
                            <dd><strong>@Model.LeadName</strong></dd>

                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.LeadCompany))
                            {
                                <dt>Company</dt>
                                <dd>@Model.LeadCompany</dd>
                            }

                            <dt>Email</dt>
                            <dd>
                                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.LeadEmail))
                                {
                                    <a href="mailto:@Model.LeadEmail">@Model.LeadEmail</a>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="text-muted">Not provided</span>
                                }
                            </dd>

                            <dt>Phone</dt>
                            <dd>
                                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.LeadPhone))
                                {
                                    <a href="tel:@Model.LeadPhone">@Model.LeadPhone</a>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="text-muted">Not provided</span>
                                }
                            </dd>

                            <dt>Status</dt>
                            @* The tenant's own name for the status, not the key. *@
                            <dd><span class="badge bg-success">@Model.LeadStatusName</span></dd>
                        </dl>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lc-card">
                    <h2><i class="bi bi-briefcase"></i>The deal</h2>
                    <div class="bd">
                        <div class="mb-3">
                            <label asp-for="Input.DealTitle" class="form-label small text-muted mb-1">
                                Deal title <span class="text-danger">*</span>
                            </label>
                            <input asp-for="Input.DealTitle" class="form-control" required maxlength="200" />
                            <span asp-validation-for="Input.DealTitle" class="text-danger small"></span>
                        </div>

                        <div class="row g-3">
                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <label asp-for="Input.ExpectedValue" class="form-label small text-muted mb-1">
                                    Expected value <span class="text-danger">*</span>
                                </label>
                                <div class="lc-money">
                                    @* The symbol for the currency the DEAL will be in —
                                       the lead's, or the workspace's. *@
                                    <span class="sym">@Model.SymbolFor(Model.DealCurrency)</span>
                                    <input asp-for="Input.ExpectedValue" type="number" step="0.01" min="0.01"
                                           class="form-control" required />
                                </div>
                                <span asp-validation-for="Input.ExpectedValue" class="text-danger small"></span>
                                <div class="form-text" style="font-size:.74rem;">
                                    In <strong>@Model.DealCurrency</strong>
                                    @if (!string.Equals(Model.DealCurrency, Model.TenantCurrency,
                                                        StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                                    {
                                        <text> — from the lead, not your workspace currency
                                        (@Model.TenantCurrency).</text>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <text> — your workspace currency.</text>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <label asp-for="Input.ExpectedCloseDate" class="form-label small text-muted mb-1">
                                    Expected close date <span class="text-danger">*</span>
                                </label>
                                <input asp-for="Input.ExpectedCloseDate" type="date" class="form-control" required />
                                <span asp-validation-for="Input.ExpectedCloseDate" class="text-danger small"></span>
                                <div class="form-text" style="font-size:.74rem;">
                                    Defaults to 30 days out.
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-12">
                                <label asp-for="Input.Description" class="form-label small text-muted mb-1">
                                    Description <span class="text-muted">(optional)</span>
                                </label>
                                <textarea asp-for="Input.Description" class="form-control" rows="3" maxlength="2000"
                                          placeholder="Anything the pipeline should know about this deal…"></textarea>
                                <span asp-validation-for="Input.Description" class="text-danger small"></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lc-card">
                    <h2><i class="bi bi-funnel"></i>Where it starts</h2>
                    <div class="bd">
                        @if (!stages.Any())
                        {
                            <div class="alert alert-warning mb-0 py-2 small">
                                <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>
                                Your workspace has no pipeline stages set up, so this lead can't be
                                converted yet.
                                <a asp-page="/Settings/Pipeline/Index">Add them under Settings</a> first.
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @* ★ The tenant's OWN stages, with the tenant's OWN
                               probabilities. This was four hardcoded options. *@
                            <div class="lc-stages" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Starting stage">
                                @foreach (var s in stages)
                                {
                                    <label class="lc-stage">
                                        <input type="radio" asp-for="Input.Stage" value="@s.Key" required />
                                        <span>
                                            @s.Name
                                            <span class="pct">@s.Probability%</span>
                                        </span>
                                    </label>
                                }
                            </div>
                            <span asp-validation-for="Input.Stage" class="text-danger small d-block mt-1"></span>
                            <div class="form-text mt-2" style="font-size:.74rem;">
                                These are your workspace's own stages and their own win
                                probabilities, from
                                <a asp-page="/Settings/Pipeline/Index">Settings → Pipeline</a>.
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-5">
                <div class="lc-card">
                    <h2><i class="bi bi-signpost-2"></i>What happens next</h2>
                    <div class="bd">
                        <ol class="lc-next ps-3 mb-0">
                            <li>A deal is created in your pipeline at the stage you chose.</li>
                            <li>
                                @* The old page said the status becomes "Converted" — our key.
                                   The tenant may well call it something else. *@
                                This lead is closed out and moves to your workspace's converted
                                status, so it stops appearing in the active list.
                            </li>
                            @if (!Model.ContactId.HasValue)
                            {
                                <li>A contact is created for @Model.LeadName automatically.</li>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <li>The deal is linked to the contact this lead already has.</li>
                            }
                            <li>You land on the pipeline board with the new deal on it.</li>
                        </ol>

                        <div class="alert alert-light border small mt-3 mb-0">
                            <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i>
                            The lead's notes, activities and tasks carry across and stay readable on
                            the deal — nothing is lost. Converting cannot be undone from here.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lc-card">
                    <h2><i class="bi bi-lightbulb"></i>Worth knowing</h2>
                    <div class="bd">
                        <ul class="lc-next ps-3 mb-0 text-muted">
                            <li>The close date drives your pipeline forecast, so a realistic one is
                                worth more than an optimistic one.</li>
                            <li>You can change the title, value and close date on the deal afterwards.</li>
                            <li>The stage can be changed on the deal page — through your process,
                                not a dropdown.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lc-bar">
            <a href="/Leads/Detail/@Model.LeadId" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Cancel</a>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-success" @(stages.Any() ? "" : "disabled")>
                <i class="bi bi-arrow-right-circle me-1"></i>Create the deal
            </button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>

@section Scripts {
    <partial name="_ValidationScriptsPartial" />
}
